# Business Process Analyst
  text: We pursue bold ideas, embrace complexity, and keep pushing forward.
  text: We act with urgency, deliver with excellence, and always find a way.
  text: We engage with empathy, align around what's best for Veracyte, and celebrate as one team.
  text: We show up with integrity, kindness, and respect for one another.
# The Position:
  text: We are seeking a motivated Business Process Analyst to support Reimbursement Operations through process improvement, workflow optimization, 
  text: The ideal candidate possesses strong analytical and process mapping skills and has experience supporting healthcare operations. This role wi
  text: Process Improvement & Operational Excellence
  text: Analyze end-to-end revenue cycle workflows and identify opportunities to reduce manual effort, rework, and process variation.
  text: Document current-state and future-state business processes using process maps, swimlane diagrams, and workflow documentation.
  text: Conduct root-cause analysis to identify operational bottlenecks, delays, and quality issues.
  text: Contribute to the development of recommendations to improve efficiency, scalability, compliance, and customer experience.
  text: Collaborate with operational teams to standardize and optimize workflows across Reimbursement Operations.
  text: Business Analysis & Requirements Management
  text: Gather and document business requirements for operational and technology initiatives.
  text: Create process flows, business requirements documents (BRDs), user stories, and acceptance criteria.
  text: Support prioritization of enhancement requests and process improvement opportunities.
  text: Perform impact assessments for proposed operational and system changes.
  text: Assist business stakeholders in defining success metrics and operational KPIs.
  text: Systems & Integration Support
  text: Assist in documenting system integration requirements and operational workflows between platforms.
  text: Collaborate with IT teams, vendors, and business users to ensure solutions meet operational needs.
  text: Participate in testing, validation, and user acceptance activities.
  text: Project Support & Collaboration
  text: Participate in stakeholder meetings, process workshops, and requirements gathering sessions.
  text: Track project deliverables, risks, issues, and action items.
  text: Communicate recommendations, findings, and project updates to operational leadership.
  text: Support organizational change management and adoption of new processes.
# Who You Are:
  text: Bachelor's degree in Business Administration, Healthcare Administration, Information Systems, Healthcare Informatics, or related field.
  text: 1-3 years of experience in business analysis, process improvement, healthcare operations, revenue cycle, or related roles.
  text: Experience documenting business processes and identifying operational improvement opportunities.
  text: Strong analytical, problem-solving, and critical-thinking skills.
  text: Excellent communication and stakeholder management abilities.
  text: Proficiency in Microsoft Excel, PowerPoint, and process mapping tools.
  text: Experience in healthcare revenue cycle management, payer operations, diagnostics, laboratory services, or healthcare technology.
  text: The final salary offered to a successful candidate will be dependent on several factors that may include but are not limited to years of exp
